  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A membership with a null `sprk_enddate`, or one dated today or later, still confers inherited access — and a named test pins it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A membership whose `sprk_enddate` has passed confers NOTHING while its `statecode` is still active — and a named test pins it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">🔴 D-10 (2026-09-21), the mirror at the other end of the range: a membership whose `sprk_startdate` is in the FUTURE confers NOTHING while `statecode` is active, a `sprk_startdate` of TODAY or NULL still confers, and the deny-veto subject is NOT start-date-bounded either. Named tests pin all three. Verified here for the same reason ISS-020 is — this file is where the date-bounding contract is checked end to end, and D-10 makes the bound two-sided. If 109 implemented only the end bound, that is a GAP to report, not a test to add here.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An org-keyed deny row STILL matches a subject whose membership ended by date (part 2: the wall over-matches by design) — and a named test pins the over-match explicitly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The conferring set and the wall-subject set come from ONE junction read, asserted by a read-count test, preserving task 043's single-snapshot invariant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The before-state required by part 3 is recorded — the count AND the list of date-ended-but-active rows — before the behaviour shipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No second junction query, second outcome record, or parallel date-bounding path exists anywhere (verified by grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ISS-020 disposition row in `notes/defer-issues.md` cites the tests and the before-state; **#999** is closed; both status artifacts agree and `check-task-status-drift.ps1` exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: this task adds no new tests of its own — it names the tests task 109 shipped. If a criterion needs a test that does not exist, that is a gap to report, not a test to add here.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Rewritten 2026-09-19 (session 17) via /task-create. Was a deliberate stub carrying the unverified-premises warning, an `&lt;owner-question status="UNDECIDED"&gt;` block, and **no `&lt;steps&gt;` element** — which made `pwsh scripts/Validate-TaskPoml.ps1 projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks` exit 1 from session 15 until now. That validator is invoked manually and is NOT wired into `/push-to-github` (Step 1.65 gates on the drift script only), which is why six broken POMLs sat unnoticed.

Part 4 of ISS-020 — the deactivation writer — is task **117**, shared with D-1 option B and ISS-026's write half. Once 117 has run, `statecode` alone is the truth and this task's date comparison becomes belt-and-braces rather than load-bearing. Keep it: it is the fail-closed half.

Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-020. Related: tasks 020, 042, 043, 109, 117.</notes>

